    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="1111" n="953" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg953"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé Hitt</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-07-20"><hi rendition="#italic">July 20,
                        1906</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 114.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith a copy of a letter from
                    the Secretary of Agriculture, transmitting correspondence between Messrs. Armour
                    &amp; Co., of Chicago, and the Italian consulate in that city, in regard to the
                    inspection of meat and meat products shipped to Italy, by examiners appointed by
                    the Italian consulate-general at New York, at the expense of the exporters.</p>
                <p>You are requested to convey to the Italian Government the information contained
                    in the letter of the Secretary of Agriculture.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>







